  <prompt>
    Materialize the advisory comments into the Compose document: emit a compose_advisory_comments event over the
    PaneEventBus (ADR-030) from the ledgered NDA-REVIEW result, and add a receiver that reuses createThread +
    resolveTargetSpans('strict') to place a Tiptap comment on each flagged clause range, with the comment text =
    the AI advisory explanation. Mirror the existing compose_qa_highlight client-event pattern.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    SPAARKE Compose client developer. Expert in Tiptap/ProseMirror, the CommentAnchorMark, useComposeCommentThreads
    (createThread, importThreads, resolveTargetSpans), and the PaneEventBus receiver pattern.
  </role>

  <goal>
    A completed NDA-REVIEW causes advisory comments to appear on the correct flagged ranges in the Compose editor,
    each carrying the AI explanation, via a lightweight client-event path (not a new routable server disposition).
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Reuse-first: compose_qa_highlight is the precedent client-event path. useComposeCommentThreads already exposes
      createThread + resolveTargetSpans('strict'); CommentAnchorMark renders the highlight span. The comments payload
      comes from task 023's fan-out. This is NOT a new server disposition — the Action output is ledgered (ADR-040)
      and the client materializes comments from it.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/hooks/useComposeCommentThreads.ts</file>
      <file>src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/useComposeWorkspaceReceivers.ts</file>
      <file>src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/ComposeEditor.tsx</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>023 (advisory-comments payload). Feeds 032 (gutter layout) + 040 (export).</dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-030">The event rides the typed PaneEventBus channel (compose_advisory_comments); follow the typed-channel contract.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-040">Comments derive from the ledgered result; do not trigger a new model call on the client.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-049">Comment anchoring uses the existing CommentAnchorMark + resolveTargetSpans('strict'); ranges that fail strict resolution are reported, not silently dropped.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Mirror the compose_qa_highlight event+receiver shape exactly. The receiver reuses createThread + resolveTargetSpans — do NOT reimplement anchoring. Each comment's text is the AI advisory explanation for that flagged section.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-030-pane-event-bus.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-040-session-ledger.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-049-compose-shadow-document.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-033-streaming-chat-tool-side-channel.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/ui/fluent-v9-component-authoring.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="compose_qa_highlight client event" location="src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/useComposeWorkspaceReceivers.ts">
        Copy this event+receiver shape; swap payload to advisory comments and place threads instead of highlights.
      </pattern>
      <pattern name="Comment threading" location="src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/hooks/useComposeCommentThreads.ts">
        Reuse createThread + resolveTargetSpans('strict') to anchor each comment.
      </pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Trace compose_qa_highlight from emission through the receiver to the editor decoration.</step>
    <step order="2">Define the compose_advisory_comments event payload (flaggedSections → {targetText/range, explanation}).</step>
    <step order="3">Emit the event from the ledgered NDA-REVIEW result.</step>
    <step order="4">Add the receiver: for each flagged section, resolveTargetSpans('strict') → createThread with the advisory explanation as the comment text.</step>
    <step order="5">Report ranges that fail strict resolution (surface count in the summary panel / console) rather than dropping silently.</step>
    <step order="6">Verify comments appear on the correct clauses with the right text; run UI tests.</step>
    <step order="7">Update TASK-INDEX.md: mark 031 ✅.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If strict anchor resolution fails for most flagged ranges (systemic, not incidental), STOP and escalate — the NDA-REVIEW output's range contract (task 020) likely needs adjustment rather than loosening anchoring to 'fuzzy'.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <tools>
    <tool name="npm">Build the shared Compose lib + code page.</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/useComposeWorkspaceReceivers.ts (advisory-comments receiver)</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a completed NDA-REVIEW, when the event fires, then advisory comments appear on the flagged clause ranges with text = the AI explanation.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Comments are created via createThread + resolveTargetSpans('strict') (existing hooks; no new anchoring code).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Ranges failing strict resolution are reported (count surfaced), not silently dropped.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No new server disposition and no client-side model call are introduced.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <ui-tests>
    <test name="Advisory comments materialize">
      <url>https://{org}.crm.dynamics.com/main.aspx?pagetype=webresource&amp;webresourceName=sprk_SpaarkeAi</url>
